prompt:
You are working with an existing note storage system. First create the notes data, then perform a retrieval and synthesis task.

Step 1: Create memory/notes/notes.json with these 5 notes:
[
  {"id": "NOTE-001", "content": "CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost) is total spend divided by new customers. High CAC with low LTV is unsustainable.", "topic": "growth-metrics", "project": "product-strategy", "created_at": "2026-03-01"},
  {"id": "NOTE-002", "content": "LTV (Lifetime Value) = ARPU * gross margin * average customer lifespan. LTV:CAC ratio above 3 is generally healthy.", "topic": "growth-metrics", "project": "product-strategy", "created_at": "2026-03-05"},
  {"id": "NOTE-003", "content": "Churn rate: monthly churn above 5% signals product-market fit issues. Net Revenue Retention above 100% means expansion revenue covers churn.", "topic": "growth-metrics", "project": "product-strategy", "created_at": "2026-03-10"},
  {"id": "NOTE-004", "content": "Payback period: how many months to recover CAC from gross profit per customer. Industry standard is under 12 months for SaaS.", "topic": "growth-metrics", "project": "product-strategy", "created_at": "2026-03-15"},
  {"id": "NOTE-005", "content": "North Star Metric should capture the core value your product delivers. For Slack it is DAU, for Airbnb it is nights booked.", "topic": "product-analytics", "project": "product-strategy", "created_at": "2026-03-20"}
]

Step 2: Find all notes related to the topic 'growth-metrics' and save search results to search_results.json:
{
  "query": "growth-metrics",
  "matched_note_ids": ["NOTE-XXX", ...],
  "count": <number>
}

Step 3: Synthesize the growth-metrics notes into a coherent framework and save to synthesis.json:
{
  "topic": "growth-metrics",
  "framework_title": "<title>",
  "key_concepts": [
    {"name": "<metric name>", "definition": "<one sentence>", "source_note": "NOTE-XXX"}
  ],
  "relationships": ["<relationship statement>", ...],
  "summary": "<2-3 sentence synthesis paragraph>"
}
Requirements: key_concepts must include CAC, LTV, churn_rate, and payback_period (4 concepts minimum). relationships must have at least 2 entries describing how metrics relate to each other.
